{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand","id":791052,"title":"Slasher Chronicles and United We Stand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-22T13:35:22-08:00","id":791052,"title":"Slasher Chronicles and United We Stand","content":"One of the core themes of Hunter has always been the power of the group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theme section from Hunter Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game has a minor theme, too: humankind is both powerful and fragile. He is fragile when he is alone and ignorant, but he is powerful when he gathers his resources and finds knowledge. Hunters must work together to accomplish their goals, but even then, a cell, compact or conspiracy is only as strong as the weakest within \u2014 one traitorous worm boring to the heart of the apple or one rogue ant that leads the trail astray has the potential to destroy the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now Slashers forming within the group and perhaps destroying it are nothing new, the very next sentence from the quoted block is <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the pressures of the Vigil, the sacrifices inherent, can drive even a hunter of the strongest heart to such disunity and disarray. </div> </div> </div>But there is a question nagging at my mind, and that question is: How would a group who wants to keep the focus on their Cell/Compact/Conspiracy <b>united</b> against monsters play in the framework of the Slasher Chronicles?<br /> <br /> Would you mostly ignore what makes Hunter 2E into the Slasher Chronicle and maybe just throw a few more Slashers into your motley mix of Vampires, Werewolves, Witches and assorted prey or is there hooks in the framework you can hang your united hunter group on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T17:20:56-08:00","id":791165,"title":"","content":"I think there is some fun to be had in playing the game with the risk of your PC becoming a Slasher... For me part of the draw of Wraith is the risk of becoming a Spectre and let's be fair, your Hunter in 1e could easily become a vampire, promethean, changeling, geist or possessed (inferno) in the run of play if the story and bad dice rolling brings it. However I suppose it depends on your PC's cell if your PC happens to become a Slasher if they keep them around and use that crazy mad violence of theirs to some advantage or not.<br /> <br /> Having a playable Slasher would be something I'd happily take some glee from in a game... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T02:43:31-08:00","id":791446,"title":"","content":"Slashers are meant to be for Hunters like the Strixs are for Vampires- something which disrupts the natural course of things, in every theme. For a united group, Slashers are the worst case scenario- they are traitors to the Vigil who turn upon mankind, they threat upon the group's very way of life and reason to exist. Things get worse if the Slasher actually follows the group's code, and that he would distinguish his &quot;friends&quot; from the rest of humanity- for it would makes them ask questions about what is the true meaning of the Vigil, and where exactly does the line cross.<br /> <br /> In sort, I think that such a group would work fine in 2E, simply because Slashers works against their very theme and would turn them into a constant threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T03:17:59-08:00","id":791459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there is a question nagging at my mind, and that question is: How would a group who wants to keep the focus on their Cell/Compact/Conspiracy <b>united</b> against monsters play in the framework of the Slasher Chronicles? </div> </div> </div>Probably not great. I mean, if you don't want to engage with the basic conflict of the game, that's kinda a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T08:34:27-08:00","id":791608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand?p=791446#post791446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slashers are meant to be for Hunters like the Strixs are for Vampires- something which disrupts the natural course of things</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the sound of that.<br /> <br /> If the natural order of things is Hunter vs Monster and slashers are a disruption that the ST might or might not throw at you - well the natural order will by definition get plenty of support.<br /> <br /> But is the quoted block something Monica has said and I missed or just speculating based on Vampire?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand?p=791459#post791459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not great. I mean, if you don't want to engage with the basic conflict of the game, that's kinda a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still consider the basic conflict of the game to be Hunters vs Monsters; not Hunter vs his inner demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T08:51:22-08:00","id":791616,"title":"","content":"well, actually it is a quote of how Dave (from Mage) defined the Chronicle books- that the point of the featured Antagonist is to be a &quot;game changer&quot;, something that starts a story in an unpredictable way and draws the protagonist from her daily life into an &quot;irregular conflict&quot;. If you look at the other antagonists, it seems like it is the direction in the rest of the games- strixs, idigam, firestorms, huntsmen and even the mysteries of the Fallen are not common phenomena in the life of the regular supernatural, and when they do show up things they shake they whole society of the shadow world. I have no reason to assume things would be different for Hunter. Anyway, Monica has said that she would make a blog post on &quot;how Slashers fit 2E&quot;, so I assume we'll know better then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:57:40-08:00","id":791684,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible that you can incorporate the slasher as a friendly NPC that goes bad, or as something a higher up asks them to hunt. There's nothing so far that forces you to make your players play a slasher against their will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T11:44:18-08:00","id":791716,"title":"","content":"To me, Slashers should be guys that went with creed of Cell/Compacts/Conspiracy to such extend that they &quot;betray&quot; it, even if technically, they still follow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T21:55:52-08:00","id":791974,"title":"","content":"My main thing with friends is how is this going to effect the Hunter vs. Monsters thematic. They've read the blog posts and various things on the net and they point to writers/devs saying that Slashers have been made more core to Hunter and shifting the focus to them away from the monster thematics. More than the other game-changers like Strix/Idigam have been. I hope this isn't true, and just wanted to hear something to assuage that fear.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T02:26:20-08:00","id":792057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand?p=791974#post791974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main thing with friends is how is this going to effect the Hunter vs. Monsters thematic. They've read the blog posts and various things on the net and they point to writers/devs saying that Slashers have been made more core to Hunter and shifting the focus to them away from the monster thematics. More than the other game-changers like Strix/Idigam have been. I hope this isn't true, and just wanted to hear something to assuage that fear.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You realize there's been like two blog posts and stuff right? And neither suggest that their will be less monsters in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T02:37:48-08:00","id":792060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still consider the basic conflict of the game to be Hunters vs Monsters; not Hunter vs his inner demons. </div> </div> </div>I mean conflict in a narrative sense. Like Requiem can be about pretty much anything, but underlying it is a conflict around maintaining your humanity. In the same way, that original quote gave one of Hunter's key underlying theme. Your teamwork is your strength (and mechanically you get to use tactics as a result) but it's a strenght underpinned by the willingness to trust others.<br /> <br /> Basically if your theme is unity in the face of adversity, you really need to show the possibility of disunity for that to have much weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:36:25-08:00","id":793106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand?p=792060#post792060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean conflict in a narrative sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> In that case I would still say I consider the basic conflict to be Hunter vs monster. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand?p=792060#post792060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically if your theme is unity in the face of adversity, you really need to show the possibility of disunity for that to have much weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. This is completely true but a valid way of showing disunity is through the monsters. If the Hunters defeat supernaturally powerful monsters because they're united and the monsters are not that demonstrates the theme nicely.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still if what LostLight's saying is accurate than it addresses all my concerns neatly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T16:44:12-08:00","id":793312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/791052-slasher-chronicles-and-united-we-stand?p=793106#post793106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In that case I would still say I consider the basic conflict to be Hunter vs monster. <br /> <br /> Sure. This is completely true but a valid way of showing disunity is through the monsters. If the Hunters defeat supernaturally powerful monsters because they're united and the monsters are not that demonstrates the theme nicely.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still if what LostLight's saying is accurate than it addresses all my concerns neatly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd have to disagree a bit. I feel that that just lacks a certain edge, and makes that conflict in particular less personal. It never becomes an issue the Hunters themselves ever have to face, it is always a conflict burdening 'the other guys', as it were. <br /> <br /> Personally, I would love a common narrative + mechanics for Hunters having to ride the thin, blurry line of morality. Performing their duty to the best of their ability but always having to worry about going too far and starting down that slippery slope to the path of Slasherdom. <br /> <br /> I mean you're already killing for the good of humanity, what happens when you run across some normal humans, be they cultists with no supernatural powers to their name or the dregs of society, the worst mankind has to offer who prey upon the innocent as surely as any witch or Werewolf? A lot of Hunters, even (especially?) players characters will eventually face that decision, and a lot of them will choose to deal with the bad guys the same as usual. <br /> <br /> And that's when they start down the slope, because after they've done it once in the name of the Code, why not do it again? And at what point do you draw the line between an acceptable level of human malevolence and when you need to Hunt? Different Hunters will surely come to different conclusions, and some of those conclusions will undoubtedly put them on the road to becoming a Slasher. I would love for this struggle to be more thoroughly represented mechanically in 2e Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}